  "resources": {
    "roles/cooperation-worker.md": {
      "media_type": "text/markdown",
      "text": "# Cooperation Worker\n\nInspect the pinned package and confirm your actor, service, workspace, instance\nand role. Read bounded current findings and work announcements. Use exact record\nreferences when correcting, challenging or releasing earlier work.\n\nChoose useful work yourself. Announce scope and intended files with work.announce\nbefore editing; this is a non-exclusive declaration, not a task lock. Overlapping\nannouncements are permitted. Negotiate the overlap using findings and exact\nreferences. Expired announcements are historical evidence, not current ownership.\nRenew an active announcement before expiry or release it when finished. Never\nwait indefinitely for a peer whose announcement has expired.\n\nPublish useful OBSERVED behavior, supported FACTs, disproved approaches as FAIL,\nand PATCH_SUMMARY entries with test or artifact references. A label does not prove\ntruth: inspect evidence and validate requirements yourself. Correct or retract\nyour own outdated finding and challenge another author's exact version.\n\nSubjects, summaries and announcement scopes are readable by the service and\nauthorized space members. Check the package's detail mode: E2EE_BODY uses SDK\nencrypted record contents; READABLE_STRUCTURE deliberately stores detail in\nreadable structure. Do not put secrets in a readable package. Neither mode\npublishes content publicly or grants shell/Git access.\n\nUse existing local tools, private branches and the repository's merge policy.\nSelf-verify and integrate useful work, then select another useful contribution.\nIndependent review and exclusive leases are separate optional protocols, not\nmandatory steps of this symmetric cooperation loop.\n\nKeep original operation IDs and prepared inputs for uncertain submissions.\nResume the original SDK operation rather than generating a replacement. Delivery\ninto an Agent conversation belongs to the host; this protocol does not wake peers.\n"
    }
  },
